{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/spread"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/spread","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"spread","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLWedgeV6spreadSdSgvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spread","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spread","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"spread","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The spread, in tenths, between the wedge lines at this point. Ignored at the start of a crescendo wedge or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the end of a diminuendo wedge.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge":{"title":"MXLWedge","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge","abstract":[{"text":"The wedge type represents crescendo and diminuendo wedge symbols. The type attribute is crescendo for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a wedge that is closed at the left side, and diminuendo for the start of a wedge that is closed on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right side. Spread values are measured in tenths; those at the start of a crescendo wedge or end of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diminuendo wedge are ignored. The niente attribute is yes if a circle appears at the point of the wedge,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicating a crescendo from nothing or diminuendo to nothing. It is no by default, and used only when the type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is crescendo, or the type is stop for a wedge that began with a diminuendo type. The line-type is solid if not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge/spread":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spread"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"spread","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/spread","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spread, in tenths, between the wedge lines at this point. Ignored at the start of a crescendo wedge or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the end of a diminuendo wedge."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/spread"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths"}}}